# Flagship interop example — `link` (SPEC.md §16)
#
# One CuNi source declares a typed HTTP+JSON contract. Compile it to Go,
# Python, and/or JavaScript: each emit produces
#   • Greet(...)           — in-process function
#   • Greet_handler        — wire handler (mount it yourself)
#   • Greet_remote(...)    — always-fallible client stub
#
# Tutorial (drivers + one-command demo):
#   docs/LINK_TUTORIAL.md
#   examples/link/demo.sh
#
# Conformance proof (Go server ← Python client over a real socket):
#   tests/conformance.rs :: link_interop_go_server_python_client
#
# Mounting the handler (port, TLS, router) is *your* job — codegen-only,
# no bundled runtime (INTEROP_PROPOSAL.md item 6).

link Greet(name: str, times: int) -> str do
    ret `hello ${name} x${times}`
end
